+/*
+ * qbt_k60.c - Redmi K60 (mondrian / SM8475 / "cape") Bluetooth board backend
+ * for the QcaBluetooth reference implementation.
+ *
+ * Target hardware (all sourced in EVIDENCE.md):
+ *   - QCA6490 / WCN6855-class controller, compatible "qcom,qca6490"
+ *   - GENI UART @ 0x00894000 (QUPV3_2 SE20), GIC SPI 587 level-high,
+ *     TLMM GPIO 76=CTS 77=RTS 78=TX 79=RX (function qup20)
+ *   - BT_EN=GPIO81, SW_CTRL=GPIO82 (input), XO latch=GPIO204, WLAN_EN=GPIO80
+ *   - BT VDD IO = PM8350 S10, 1.8 V fixed, under /soc/rsc@17a00000
+ *
+ * STATUS: EXPERIMENTAL.  Eight-step pipeline ①–⑦ are documented in
+ * REPORT.md; ⑧ (on-device) has not been executed.  Do not treat any
+ * register value as hardware-verified until the S0–S6 matrix in REPORT.md
+ * has a device log attached.
+ *
+ * This file is an implementation skeleton: every register/constant that could
+ * not be checked against a public source is marked TODO.  It does not attempt
+ * any unverified write.  Build it as a normal XNU BSD C file; for host syntax
+ * checking compile with -DK60_BT_HOST_TEST.
+ *
+ * IMPORTANT (K60-specific): never map or read the RSC (0x17a00000 /
+ * 0x17a20000).  The first RSC register read kills this machine
+ * (GOODIX-TOUCH-PORT.md:99-105).  All PMIC rails used by Bluetooth
+ * (PM8350 S10/S11/S12, PM8350C S1, PMR735A L7) are RPMh-controlled
+ * (K60 live FDT:5796-5804) and must be inherited from a warm Android boot.
+ */
